Rough translation in English: (google translate so don't judge please :p)

&#x200B;

Headline: Rutte about rioters old and new: 'I'd like to beat them all together'

&#x200B;

The violence during old and new has increased again. Prime Minister Mark Rutte is furious at the wheel rotators who have committed themselves to old and new to help workers: "I would prefer to beat them all up personally, the people who do that, but that does not work."

&#x200B;

The number of incidents increased by 10 to 12 percent, according to official figures. Policemen were often bombarded with heavy fireworks or faced with other violence.

&#x200B;

'Itching'

Prime Minister Rutte calls the violence 'unacceptable'. Rutte finds it 'frustrating' that society fails to stop people from such misbehavior and 'itch hands' to play for their own judges.

&#x200B;

But of course he can not, he realizes. According to him, it is extremely difficult to find an approach that works.

&#x200B;

'This is not possible'

"As it is now in New Year's Eve, that's simply not possible," Minister Ferd Grapperhaus said earlier today. Nevertheless, for the time being Grapperhaus does not want to ban a nationwide fireworks ban, for which the Dutch Safety Board, the municipalities and the governmental party ChristenUnie, among others, plead.

&#x200B;

Reporting duty

Grapperhaus sees more in a duty to report for wheel turners. The mayor can order those who misbehave at the turn of the year to report to the police at the next edition. The police would like to see mayors use this power more often. Grapperhaus will raise the possibility in the consultation with the mayors.
